# Drizzle migration snapshots MUST stay committed — they are not build output.
#
# `drizzle-kit generate` computes the next migration by diffing the current
# schema against the most recent snapshot. If these were gitignored, a fresh
# clone would have nothing to diff against and the next `db:generate` would
# emit a migration recreating all 21 tables on top of a database that already
# has them. `db:check` also reads them to detect journal/SQL drift — the exact
# breakage that made `db:migrate` hang before migration 0001 was repaired.
#
# They are large (a full schema snapshot each, not a delta) and nobody should
# read them, so mark them generated: GitHub collapses generated files in pull
# request diffs by default. Committed, but not review surface.
#
# This affects GitHub's rendering only — local `git diff` is unchanged.
db/migrations/meta/*.json linguist-generated=true

# The SQL files are deliberately NOT marked: every one of them runs against
# production and must be read line by line in review.

package-lock.json linguist-generated=true
